WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.142 --> 00:00:07.742
This is how you write a blog post in the Fixer Nation admin. From the Blog page, choose New Post.

2
00:00:08.243 --> 00:00:16.243
Start with a title. The slug, which is the end of the web address, fills in for you. You can change it if you want something shorter.

3
00:00:16.743 --> 00:00:22.963
Add a category, and a one or two line excerpt. That's the text people see on the blog index.

4
00:00:23.463 --> 00:00:30.033
The body works like a word processor. What you see here uses the same spacing as the published page.

5
00:00:30.535 --> 00:00:35.335
Use the heading buttons for section titles, and bold or italic for emphasis.

6
00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:39.534
Lists, quotes and divider lines are one click each.

7
00:00:40.036 --> 00:00:44.946
To add a link, highlight the words, click Link, and enter the address when asked.

8
00:00:45.448 --> 00:00:49.588
Click Image to upload a picture. It goes straight into the post.

9
00:00:50.089 --> 00:00:53.789
The alignment buttons let you center or justify text.

10
00:00:54.290 --> 00:01:01.420
Leave the publish date blank to save a draft. Nothing goes live until you set a date. Click Create Post.

11
00:01:01.919 --> 00:01:10.579
Your draft is saved. Click Preview draft to see it exactly as readers will. The spacing matches what you just saw in the editor.

12
00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:15.510
Come back any time to keep editing, then add a publish date when it's ready.
